**RECOMMENDED RAG RATINGS**
**All 5 Audit Areas**

*Multi-Dimensional Assessment Framework*
*6 Dimensions × 5 Levels*

May 2026 | Based on HoA Digital Skills & Infrastructure Audit

# EXECUTIVE SUMMARY

**Key Findings:**

All 5 areas have Digital Leads identified and staff engagement is positive. Infrastructure is adequate in most areas. The primary blockers are: (1) inadequate accessibility training & practice across all areas, (2) software/infrastructure gaps preventing movement from Level 2→1 or Level 3→2, (3) lack of systematic progress tracking (Century IA, specialist skills rubrics not embedded).

**Overall Portfolio Health:**

2 areas at Level 2 (On Track); 3 areas at Level 3 (Developing). No areas at Level 1 (Confident) or Level 5 (Urgent). This is a healthy distribution for a college-wide pilot.

**Critical Issue:**

Accessibility & Inclusion (Dimension 5) is the weakest dimension across all areas. HBH/EYE scored Level 4 (Challenged) on accessibility. All other areas need immediate Accessibility Teach-Meet training.

**Timeline:**

3 areas (BUS, HBH/EYE, SIX) can move to Level 1 within 6–8 weeks with targeted coaching. 2 areas (BUI/CON, MOT) need 8 weeks due to infrastructure barriers.

