## Key Areas of Concern

### 1. ACCESSIBILITY & INCLUSION (Dimension 5) — URGENT

**Issue: **

Accessibility is the weakest dimension across all 5 areas. HBH/EYE scored Level 4 (Challenged). No area has systematic WCAG 2.2 AA practice, proactive AT offer, or accessibility checker use.

Action: Accessibility Teach-Meet Week 2–3. All 5 areas attend. Content: WCAG 2.2 AA basics, Immersive Reader demo, Live Captions, alt text, accessible assignment design. HBH/EYE prioritized (Tracey & Sharon co-facilitate if possible).

Impact: This single intervention could move all 5 areas up on Dimension 5 within 2–3 weeks post-training.

### 2. SOFTWARE & INFRASTRUCTURE GAPS — BLOCKING LEVEL 2→1 PROGRESSION

BUS: CRM & Booking Systems training not yet started

BUI/CON & MOT: Network connectivity issues in workshop spaces; CAD/diagnostics software not fully available

SIX: Computer Science applications pending

HBH/EYE: Software licensing gaps (analytics, design tools); iPad provision timeline unclear

**Action: **

Joe A meeting (Week 1) to discuss procurement pathway for CRM, CAD, diagnostics, analytics tools. Timeline? Cost? Approval process?

### 3. SYSTEMATIC PROGRESS TRACKING NOT YET EMBEDDED

Century Initial Assessment: No area mentioned 100% completion. No dashboard monitoring in place.

Specialist Digital Skills: Not formally rubricized or tracked in Markbook across any area.

**Action: **

QUICK WIN: By Week 4, all 5 areas should have (1) 100% Century IA completion, (2) one specialist skills rubric drafted & piloted in one unit of work.

### 4. HoA LEADERSHIP & PLANNING — VARIABLE OWNERSHIP

No area has a written digital QIP target, formalized CPD pathway linked to Pyramid, or monthly tracking structure.

**Action: **

Coaching conversations Week 1–2. Use this assessment as a conversation starter. Help each HoA articulate their top 3 priorities & commit to monthly check-ins.

